    {
      "id": "STY-02",
      "chapter": "inputs",
      "title": "Integral homology stabilizes at two adjacent rank thresholds",
      "anchor": "inputs-stable-cycles",
      "statement": "In degree m, stabilization from GL_n(R) to GL_{n+1}(R) is surjective for n≥2m+s+1 and injective for n≥2m+s+2. Over a Dedekind domain, any size N≥n gives an integral isomorphism once n≥2m+4.",
      "hypotheses": "Integral group homology with trivial coefficients and commutative R of stable range at most s; the arithmetic application uses the Dedekind parameter s=2. These are sufficient thresholds. The split-sequence exactness theorem is used at length p under 2p+s+1≤b.",
      "definitions": [
        "One-rank steps use ambient size b=n+1. The position p in the sequence complex is a length, and q denotes a degree of group homology.",
        "The kernel factorizations of the differential pass lower-degree exactness to a surjective bottom map. In the larger range the image of the preceding zero map is its kernel."
      ],
